  [31, "你身体里的小队：IFS 内在部分与注意力审计", "The team inside you: IFS parts and an attention audit", "内在部分识别", "Recognising your inner parts", "心理健康教育", "ai"],
  [32, "向内探索：三个视角与变革免疫地图", "Looking inward: three perspectives and immunity to change", "主客体转换与变革免疫", "Subject-object shift and immunity to change", "心理健康教育", "ai"],
  [33, "AI 公司的「焚书坑儒」", "Who paid for the AI?", "谁为 AI 付了账：AI 伦理", "Who paid for the AI: AI ethics", "AI 伦理 · Digital Society", "ai"],
];
---

<PageBanner
  asset="banner/course-v1.webp"
  eyebrow={["产品 · 课程与工具卡", "Product · courses & thinking cards"]}
  title={[
    ["一门课，把一个思维方法", "A course coaches one thinking method"],
    ["带练到会用。", "until she can actually use it."],
  ]}
  lead={[
    "AI 互动课堂，在真实情境中带着学生学会多项思维工具的应用。每一节都是一台确定性状态机：放一段材料，等她看完，递上一张卡，等她填完，再往下走。",
    "An interactive AI classroom that teaches a set of thinking tools by using them on real material. Every slice is a deterministic state machine: play the material, wait, hand over a card, wait for her answer, move on.",
  ]}
/>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
            <Figure
        class="rv-pop"
        name="product-course-runtime"
        ratio="16-9"
        desc={t(lang, "课程播放界面全景：左侧素材、右侧旁白与工具卡、底部进度", "The course player: material, narration and card, with progress")}
        caption={t(
          lang,
          "《信息过滤神器》——一门以「可信度」为概念透镜的信息素养课，材料由学生自己的检索带进课堂。",
          "“The Information Filter” — an information-literacy course under the concept lens of credibility, where the material arrives from the student's own search.",
        )}
      />

      <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:56px">
        <div class="card rv" style="--i:0">
          <div class="cardic a"><Icon name="cards" /></div>
          <h3>{t(lang, "一张卡是一套方法", "A card is a method, packaged")}</h3>
          <p>
            {t(
              lang,
              "它把一套思维方法拆成看得见的几步。点开一张卡，AI 就从「供答者」退成「接生者」——只提问，不代产。",
              "It breaks a thinking method into visible steps. Open one and the AI steps back from answer-giver to midwife: it questions, it does not deliver.",
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card rv" style="--i:1">
          <div class="cardic a"><Icon name="hand" /></div>
          <h3>{t(lang, "召唤权在学生手里", "She holds the summons")}</h3>
          <p>
            {t(
              lang,
              "触发是自动的，打开由她确认。质疑一个 AI 不需要勇气，邀请对手同样不需要——剩下的只有想不想较真。",
              "The trigger is automatic; opening it is her call. Challenging an AI takes no courage, and neither does inviting one. What's left is whether she wants to get it right.",
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card rv" style="--i:2">
          <div class="cardic a"><Icon name="branch" /></div>
          <h3>{t(lang, "点卡这个动作自带标记", "The tap itself is data")}</h3>
          <p>
            {t(
              lang,
              "系统在触发场景递卡，记「引导」；无人提示、她自己召唤，记「自发」。A2 与 A4 的证据，就采在这一点之差。",
              "Offered by the system: logged as prompted. Summoned with nobody asking: logged as self-initiated. The whole A2/A4 signal lives in that one difference.",
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rv" style="margin-top:64px">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:18px"><span class="pip"></span>{t(lang, "34 张卡 · 一门课通常只用三到五张", "34 cards · a course usually uses three to five")}</div>
        <div class="marquee">
          <div class="marquee-track">
            {[...cards, ...cards].map(([zh, en], i) => (
              <div class="tcard">
                <div class="tn">{String((i % cards.length) + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</div>
                <div class="tt">{t(lang, zh, en)}</div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pull rv" style="margin-top:64px; max-width:880px">
        {t(
          lang,
          "一张卡被召唤得越来越少的时候，它才算成功——与此同时，它封装的那句追问，开始出现在学生自己的提示词和修订里。",
          "A card succeeds when its summons start falling — while the question it packaged starts showing up in the student's own prompts and revisions.",
        )}
        <cite>{t(lang, "脚手架的宿命是拆除；卡片的宿命是被吸收为内心的声音。", "Scaffolding is meant to come down. A card is meant to become an inner voice.")}</cite>
      </div>

      <!-- lenses -->
      <div class="sec-head rv" style="margin-top:80px">
        <div class="eyebrow"><span class="pip"></span>{t(lang, "学科透镜", "Disciplinary lenses")}</div>
        <h2 class="sub-title" style="margin-top:14px">
          {t(lang, "同一段材料，换一个透镜，看见的东西就不同", "Same material, different lens, different thing seen")}
        </h2>
        <p class="body" style="margin-top:14px">
          {t(
            lang,
            "透镜只规定你在原文里找什么，答案仍然要自己得出——所以每一次使用都要落回一句具体的话、一处别人可以核对的证据。",
            "A lens only tells you what to look for in the text; the answer is still yours to reach. So every use has to land on one specific sentence someone else can check.",
          )}
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tablewrap rv" style="margin-top:32px">
        <table class="dt">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th style="width:150px">{t(lang, "透镜", "Lens")}</th>
              <th>{t(lang, "它追问什么", "What it interrogates")}</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {lenses.map(([zh, en, dz, de]) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="k">{t(lang, zh, en)}</td>
                <td>{t(lang, dz, de)}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- the catalogue: every course we actually run -->
  <section class="section band-paper">
    <div class="container" data-catalog>
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <div class="eyebrow"><span class="pip"></span>{t(lang, "课程库", "The catalogue")}</div>
        <h2 class="sec-title">
          <span data-count="33">33</span>{t(lang, " 门课，每一门都对得上某张官方评分表", " courses, each mapped onto a real mark scheme")}
        </h2>
        <p class="lead">
          {t(
            lang,
            "一门课通常只用到三到五张工具卡。选课不按学科分，按学生这学期最缺的那一样能力分。",
            "A course usually calls on three to five cards. They aren't sorted by subject but by the ability a student is short of this term.",
          )}
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="catbar rv" style="margin-top:34px">
        {courseTags.map(([k, zh, en], i) => (
          <button class="catbtn" type="button" data-tag={k} aria-pressed={i === 0 ? "true" : "false"}>
            {t(lang, zh, en)}
          </button>
        ))}
        <span class="catcount" data-catcount data-catcount-tpl={t(lang, "{n} 门", "{n} courses")}></span>
      </div>

      <div class="catgrid rv">
        {courseList.map(([n, zh, en, fz, fe, sysx, tags]) => (
          <article class="catcard" data-tags={tags}>
            <div class="cn">{String(n).padStart(2, "0")}</div>
            <h4>{t(lang, zh, en)}</h4>
            <div class="cf">{t(lang, fz, fe)}</div>
            <div class="cs">
              {sysx.split(" · ").map((x) => <span>{x}</span>)}
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

<CtaBand />

<Pager links={[
    {
      href: "/product/projects",
      kicker: ["下一面", "Next"],
      title: ["探究性写作空间", "The inquiry writing space"],
      body: ["把课上练会的方法，用在自己的真实课题上", "Take the method you practised into coursework of your own"],
    },
    {
      href: "/product",
      kicker: ["返回", "Back"],
      title: ["产品总览", "Product overview"],
      body: ["四个部分，合起来是一条完整链路", "Four parts, one path end to end"],
    },
  ]} />
